{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>The first of the first fruits of your land</b> — Because He mentioned that they shall bring the first fruits of all that is in their land to the house of YHWH, He adjoined to this <b>you shall not boil a kid in its mother's milk</b>, for at the time of the first fruits of the land they will also bring every firstborn of the animals, the kids and the lambs, and at that time the kids will have grown and there will be milk, and many times the mother will go up with the firstborn while it is still nursing, so that it will not die. Now those who come for the festival will indulge to eat the firstlings with all delicacies together with the priests, and therefore He mentioned their prohibition along with the first fruits. But in Mishneh Torah (Deuteronomy 14:21) He mentioned this commandment along with the prohibition of foods, after He mentioned unclean animals and fish and unclean birds and carrion, for there it is fitting to mention this, since it is a prohibition of food, not a prohibition of cooking alone, as those of little faith who lack understanding would think."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:21:32.728918982Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}